///| The one `chrome.*` API factory every MV3 extension context is built from (`extensions.pion` / `extensions_sw.pion`):
///| content scripts (isolated world, `ctx: 'content'`), extension pages such as the toolbar popup and options page
///| (their own main world, `ctx: 'page'`) and the background service worker (its own OS-thread isolate,
///| `ctx: 'worker'`). Each context hands it `call(a, b, payload)`: host op 135 (synchronous, wrapped in a Promise)
///| in a page or isolated world, a `postMessage` RPC answered by the host's pump in the worker. Every API returns a
///| Promise and also takes Chrome's trailing callback. The factory returns:
///|   `{ chrome, dispatch, deliver, fire, portConnect, portMessage, portDisconnect }`.
///|
///| Op 135 sub-codes (`a`; `b` is the storage area, the tab id, or the sender kind):
///|   1-4 storage get/set/remove/clear (b: 0 local, 1 sync, 2 session),
///|   10 runtime.sendMessage (b: 0 content, 1 worker, 2 extension page), 11 deferred async reply,
///|   20/21 declarativeNetRequest,
///|   30-36 tabs (query, sendMessage, get, create, update, remove, reload),
///|   40-49 action (setBadgeText, getBadgeText, setBadgeBackgroundColor, getBadgeBackgroundColor, setTitle, getTitle,
///|     setPopup, getPopup, enable/disable, isEnabled; b: tab id or -1),
///|   50-54 alarms (create, get, getAll, clear, clearAll),
///|   60-65 scripting (executeScript, insertCSS, removeCSS, registerContentScripts, unregisterContentScripts,
///|     getRegisteredContentScripts),
///|   70-73 contextMenus (create, update, remove, removeAll),
///|   80 runtime.openOptionsPage, 81-84 permissions (contains, getAll, request, remove),
///|   85 commands.getAll, 86-88 offscreen (createDocument, closeDocument, hasDocument),
///|   89 windows (b: 0 getCurrent, 1 getLastFocused, 2 getAll, 3 create, 4 update, 5 remove),
///|   90 cross-world DOM event forwarding,
///|   91-95 Ports & Native Messaging (connect, port.postMessage, port.disconnect, connectNative, sendNativeMessage),
///|   100 SW fetch(). Answers are JSON; `{"__fvError": msg}` rejects the Promise.

fn ext_chrome_api_factory_js() -> String {
  let src =
  #|(function (host) {
